  "scope_boundary": "Configured routes/catalog do not attest real provider authorization/capacity; readiness is dependency readiness without completions, not dispatch authority. No publication or current-main hosted gate claimed.",
  "source_findings": [
    "preview_plan accepts actual Plan and EffortRouter, validates explicit mapping types/keys, visits every authored part via route_for and idempotency_key, uses ready_parts(()) and reports step_up only as metadata.",
    "Both helper and CLI serialize the whole report with native canonical_json and enforce report size before delivery; CLI raw hashes bind capped captured UTF-8 input bytes.",
    "CLI parses strict JSON/native Plan, validates configured routes through Route and EffortRouter, and rejects unauthorized explicit routes even on dependency-blocked parts before success serialization.",
    "Input reads use a file descriptor and regular-file metadata with capped reads; no Ledger, Hub, dispatcher, provider, socket or child process is called by the new module.",
    "File output stages in the destination parent, writes/flushes/fsyncs before no-clobber os.link, removes only its owned stage, and performs no success stdout step. If cleanup fails after publication the source explicitly reports that publication occurred; this postpublication failure was inspected, not simulated.",
    "Stdout explicitly flushes and handles OSError, redirecting the descriptor to devnull to prevent a second failed shutdown flush; the actual /dev/full receiver exits 2 without traceback."
